<h4 id="encoding-and-decoding-serializing-to-json">Encoding and Decoding (Serializing to JSON)</h4>

<p>All the code above uses @AppStorage to store basic data types. But what if it’s a Person object?</p>

<p>To be used with @AppStorage (i.e., UserDefault), it must implement encoding and decoding. Similar to how NSObject needs to conform to the Copy protocol, in Swift this is a synthesized protocol called <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Codable</code>, which includes Decodable &amp; Encodable.</p>

